[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/entities/leg_snow.gd" id="1_legsnow"]

; The snow a walker carries out of a drift, and sheds step by step.
;
; A SCENE AND NOT A NODE IN scenes/main.tscn, and registered as an autoload
; rather than placed. Two reasons, and the second is the one that matters:
;
;   * It is not a place in the world. Both emitters run in WORLD space and are
;     positioned by the footfall that made them, so this node's own transform is
;     nothing but a culling box that follows the walker.
;   * It finds its subject through the ServiceRegistry -- the same way
;     OccluderFader, which is also an autoload and also a rendering system, finds
;     the same subject. So it works in scenes/main.tscn and in every capture
;     harness under tools/ without either of them naming it.
;
; A second walker -- the bear in Wave 4, the hungry man in Wave 5 -- gets leg
; snow by registering itself as a service and instancing this scene with
; `subject_service` pointed at it. No `.gd` changes anywhere.

[node name="LegSnow" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_legsnow")
